{% set q = data.quality %}
# Cleaning log

| Step | Decision | Rows affected |
|---|---|---|
| Whitespace | Trim leading/trailing spaces in every text field | all |
| Duplicates | Drop exact duplicate rows from the full file before splitting | {{ q.duplicates_removed }} |
| `TotalCharges` blanks | Blank strings become missing; customers with tenure 0 get 0 (they have not been billed yet) | {{ q.total_charges_filled_zero }} of {{ q.total_charges_missing_before }} |
| Other numeric gaps | Median imputation fitted on train inside the model pipeline; the same train medians fill gaps before valuing customers | 0 in the source |
| `SeniorCitizen` | Normalised to the strings "0"/"1" | all |
| Label | `Churn` Yes/No mapped to `churn` 1/0; not used as a feature | all |
| Service consistency | "No phone service" / "No internet service" kept as their own categories and checked against the parent service; as model inputs they count as "does not have the service" | 0 violations |
| Extended-sample join | Join on customer ID only after every shared field agrees; keep churn reason (churners only) and CLTV in a separate file; map the {{ reasons.by_reason | length }} reasons to IBM's five categories | {{ extended.join.matched | num }} matched |
| Outliers | Valid extreme values kept; nothing trimmed | 0 |
| Split | Stratified 60/20/20 train/validation/test, seed {{ cfg.seed }}; IDs saved in `data/processed/splits.csv` | {{ data.splits.train | num }} / {{ data.splits.validation | num }} / {{ data.splits.test | num }} |

